Summary: Deliver WM_PAINT for composited windows straight away in one PeekMessage case
Category: input
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 19488
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/win32u/message.c
  Changes: CrossOver 26.3.0's lines verbatim, at the same place in 10.0's
    peek_message (only the context differs)
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: its win32u.so's peek_message tests that
    flag combination, WM_PAINT and WS_EX_COMPOSITED, and calls
    get_window_long and send_message_timeout (found by comparing functions,
    2026-11-15; it adds no strings, so the strings inventory missed it)
Upstream: no
Why: When a program peeks with exactly PM_REMOVE | PM_QS_INPUT |
 PM_QS_POSTMESSAGE | PM_QS_PAINT | PM_QS_SENDMESSAGE and the message is
 WM_PAINT for a WS_EX_COMPOSITED window, send WM_PAINT to the window straight
 away and keep looking without PM_QS_PAINT, instead of returning it. If the
 window procedure leaves the window invalid, a loop such as
 while (PeekMessage(...)) DispatchMessage(...) otherwise gets WM_PAINT on
 every call and never ends; with this, PeekMessage returns FALSE once the
 queue has nothing else. Posted and sent messages arrive either way.
Programs: none known; a program whose PeekMessage loop uses exactly these
 flags over a WS_EX_COMPOSITED window that leaves itself invalid
 (CrossOver's hack names none)
Known issues: WH_GETMESSAGE hooks and the program's own loop never see the
 WM_PAINT it sends, so a loop that draws when it sees WM_PAINT would stop
 drawing (no such program known).
Uncertain: which program CrossOver wrote it for, and whether Windows behaves
 this way. The flags must match exactly: PM_QS_INPUT as Windows 8+ headers
 define it (with QS_TOUCH and QS_POINTER), so programs built with older
 headers, or passing PM_REMOVE alone, are unaffected. None of the likely
 candidates reaches the code path: Big Fish Game Manager, Iji, Icy
 Tower's Inno 5.1.2 installer, and the Webmaster and Bioscopia Director
 projectors made no PeekMessage call with those flags (or the pre-Windows
 8 value) and had no WS_EX_COMPOSITED window (relay probe, Sikarugir
 10.0_8, macOS 26.7.2, 2026-11-26); Steam's client wasn't tried.
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-15: not yet built (no later record)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/message.c b/dlls/win32u/message.c
index 2f1e14c..72a802e 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -2999,6 +2999,15 @@ int peek_message( MSG *msg, const struct peek_message_filter *filter )
                     info.msg.lParam = result->lparam;
                 }
             }
+            /* CXHACK 19488 */
+            if (info.msg.message == WM_PAINT &&
+                    flags == (PM_REMOVE | PM_QS_INPUT | PM_QS_POSTMESSAGE | PM_QS_PAINT | PM_QS_SENDMESSAGE) &&
+                    (get_window_long( info.msg.hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_COMPOSITED ))
+            {
+                send_message( info.msg.hwnd, info.msg.message, info.msg.wParam, info.msg.lParam );
+                flags &= ~PM_QS_PAINT;
+                continue;
+            }
             *msg = info.msg;
             msg->pt = point_phys_to_win_dpi( info.msg.hwnd, info.msg.pt );
             thread_info->client_info.message_pos   = MAKELONG( msg->pt.x, msg->pt.y );
